  {
    "id": "1887500167974211840",
    "created_at": "2025-02-06 08:54:42 -05:00",
    "full_text": "The original issuance research modeled operating costs and risks, and favoured security over shrinking supply, yes. \n\nThe current research does focus on shrinking/capping supply a lot, whether you think it orthogonal or otherwise. Meanwhile, it doesn't yet cover the costs side of the economic equation as far as I can find. \n \nhttps://t.co/IKiBobcy6L\nhttps://t.co/n2O6RMVPIy\n\nAnd if you're advocating for a change to a supposedly broken issuance curve, why do you care what they were focused on at the time when they set it? Costs, risks, and a smooth curve down to a real rate of 0% were and are good ideas.",
    "media": [],
    "screen_name": "OisinKyne",
    "name": "oisin.eth | Obol",
    "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2010090282872631296/CxH7dJDv_normal.jpg",
